  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Transboundary Water Resources Management in the Incomati-Maputo River Basins</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the GEF PPG is to develop the project concept into a full project: &#x201c;Strengthening integrated transboundary management of the Incomati and Maputo River basins. As described in the PIF, this project aims to promote integrated source-to-sea management of the Incomati and Maputo River basins and coastal zones to ensure environmental security and inclusive livelihoods. It has five components: Strengthening regional governance frameworks for transboundary basin management, including the application of a source-to-sea management approach; facilitating a knowledge-based approach for source-to-sea management; supporting basin-wide and coastal zone strategic planning and investment mobilisation; creating sustainable livelihoods through enhancing water, food, energy and environmental security; and knowledge generation, communication, and dissemination.</narrative>
  </description>
